@@ -265,3 +264,36 @@ is recorded in the PR and #67, including failed/repeated/race attempts.
 
 No new transport, shaping change, EX failover, restart-resume feature, browser
 impersonation claim or numerical blocking probability is introduced here.
+
+## Staged EX PKI and iMonitor requirements follow-up
+
+PrepareEX generates changed-host/new-install certificates in an instance-scoped
+candidate directory beside the live PKI on the same filesystem. Pairing reads
+the candidate CA; existing live config, PKI and service remain untouched. The
+candidate certificate/key, CA chain, hostname and validity time are checked
+before returning the pairing code and again before activation.
+
+Commit persists previous/candidate identities and exchange intent before moving
+trees. Existing live material and candidate are rechecked, including after the
+candidate moves to the reserved backup path. Atomic directory exchange retains
+the complete old certificate set; initial installs use a durable rename. Errors
+before/after exchange restore the verified old tree or report incomplete abort,
+without guessing the ownership of changed files. Candidate cleanup also checks
+identity; first-install absence is distinct from missing prior identity.
+
+The reproduced baseline regression failed because Prepare changed live PKI.
+Added tests cover prepared abort, candidate/live edits, symlinks, occupied backup,
+first install and injected failures before/after exchange. The real-process sibling
+fixture also sends new Bulgaria echo traffic while its replacement CA is still
+prepared, before either side commits. Exact-SHA validation is recorded separately.
+
+This closes local certificate preparation isolation, not fully staged two-node
+payload verification or atomic config/unit/PKI cutover. Noise-key creation on a
+new unconfigured instance retains its prior behavior. Old in-flight transactions
+retain their recorded layout; downgrading the binary during a NEW staged transaction
+has not been validated and is not supported. Host-wide reservation, #197 shared
+binary compatibility, real systemd deployment and authorized field gates remain.
+
+[iMonitor integration plan](imonitor-integration-plan.md) maps independently
+reviewed requirements to existing BAFT work, with explicit measurement budgets
+and acceptance criteria. No upstream source or test protocol is copied.
